        "code": "# Create a volume managed by Docker\ndocker volume create pgdata\n\n# Start PostgreSQL with its data directory stored in the volume (lab password, not a real one)\ndocker run -d --name db \\\n  -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme-in-vault \\\n  -v pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data \\\n  postgres:17-alpine\n\n# Wait until the server accepts TCP connections (the temporary init server does not), then write one row\nuntil docker exec db pg_isready -h 127.0.0.1 -q; do sleep 1; done\ndocker exec db psql -U postgres -c \"CREATE TABLE notes (txt text)\" -c \"INSERT INTO notes VALUES ('still here')\"\n\n# Destroy the container completely...\ndocker rm -f db\n\n# ...start a brand new one on the same volume: the row is back\ndocker run -d --name db -v pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data postgres:17-alpine\nuntil docker exec db pg_isready -h 127.0.0.1 -q; do sleep 1; done\ndocker exec db psql -U postgres -c \"SELECT txt FROM notes\"\n",
