      "en": "- **Named volumes** for data that must be kept; **bind mounts** for configuration and development.\n- **`:ro`** on every mount that needs no write access.\n- **Never** mount `/`, `/etc` or `/var/run/docker.sock` in an application container.\n- **One user-defined network** per application; an `--internal` network for databases.\n- **Publish only what is needed**, and state the address: `127.0.0.1:8080:8080`.\n- **Back up your volumes** (a regular `pg_dump` to external storage): a volume protects against `docker rm`, not against human error or a disk failure.\n"
